  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\to.von.neumann.natural{n}]\nDefines: m \"in\" \\von.neumann.naturals\nwhen: n is \\natural\nexpresses:\n. piecewise:\n  if: n = 0\n  then: m = \\empty.set\n  else:\n  . let: k is \\natural\n    where: n = \\naturals..S(k)\n    then: m = \\set.successor:of{\\to.von.neumann.natural{k}}\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Von Neumann Numeral Equivalent of $n?$\"\n. written: \"[n?]\"\n. description: \"The canonical map from abstract Peano naturals to their Von\n                Neumann set-theoretic numeral representatives.\"\nId: \"3aa2a394-dea8-48d6-8b73-6ad032408fe2\"",
